reading:
  scalar pair, symbol identity  : agrees with opcode multiset
  aggregate pair, symbol identity: reports NOT ERASED
  aggregate pair, opcode multiset: reports ERASED

  So the two oracles DISAGREE at the aggregate, and the disagreement is not
  a tie. The bodies compute the same thing with the same instructions in the
  same quantity; only register allocation, scheduling and label names differ,
  and a compiler is free to choose all three. Symbol identity is measuring
  something the criterion does not ask about.
